!! What it does

A zettelkasten-style note app for TiddlyWiki. Notes live under the `knowledge/…` title namespace and link via short refs (`[[Foo]]`) thanks to the [[namespace|$:/plugins/rimir/namespace]] plugin. The app provides a clear home for those notes — sidebar navigation, a Note view with backlinks, a Write-tab maintenance dashboard, and a quick-capture flow.

!! Features

* Quick-capture from the topbar — title + body modal, prepends `\context knowledge`, lands at `knowledge/inbox/<slug>`.
* Three note tiers: `fleeting` → `developing` → `evergreen`. Click the pill to promote.
* Backlinks panel reads namespace's reverse index (`ns-backlinks`).
* Write tab — orphans, stubs, dead-ends, broken refs.
* Search over title + text.
* Starter mount `kn` so any tiddler can write `[[kn/topics/foo]]` and reach knowledge content.
* Custom pseudo `_index` — inside an absolute ref, `…/_index` resolves to the topic's `index` or `README`.

!! Prerequisites

* [[appify|$:/plugins/rimir/appify]]
* [[namespace|$:/plugins/rimir/namespace]]
* [[theme|$:/plugins/rimir/theme]]

!! Quick start

# Open the FAB → "Knowledge".
# Topbar → ''+ Note''. Type a title and (optionally) some body wikitext.
# Type `[[Foo]]` somewhere to link a (possibly future) note.
# Open Write to see what needs work.

